    "q-213276": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213276",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given that $12a≡12b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,16),$ construct a statement that also must be true:\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}a≡{{field-2}}b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,{{field-3}})\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The division property of modular arithmetic states that for $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have a common factor of $k=4,$ and the congruence can be written as\n\n$$\n4\\cdot 3a≡4\\cdot 3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4\\cdot 4).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can cancel out the common factor on both sides of the congruence and the modulus:\n\n$$\n\\cancel{4}\\cdot 3a≡\\cancel{4}\\cdot 3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{4}\\cdot 4)\\,⟺\\,3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "select",
          "dom_id": "selectList-213276-0",
          "tag": "custom-select",
