    "q-103181": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103181",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Given that $5a≡5b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\nI. $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)$\n\nII. $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$\n\nIII. $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10)$",
      "worked_solution": "The division property of modular arithmetic states that for $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWe're asked to consider the following statement:\n\n$$\n5a≡5b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10)\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\text{gcd}(5,10)=5.$\n\nApplying the division property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a & ≡5b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\ 5\\cdot a & ≡5\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5\\cdot 2) \\\\ \\cancel{5}\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{5}\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{5}\\cdot 2) \\\\ a & ≡b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\".",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
