    "q-86318": {
      "dom_id": "step-q86318",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Given that $6a≡6b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,12),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\nI. $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$\n\nII. $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)$\n\nIII. $3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$",
      "worked_solution": "The division properties of modular arithmetic state the following:\n\n- For $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\n- For $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1,$ we have \n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Applying the first property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6a & ≡6b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,12) \\\\ 6\\cdot a & ≡6\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,6\\cdot 2) \\\\ \\cancel{6}\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{6}\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{6}\\cdot 2) \\\\ a & ≡b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. By statement II and the first property, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)\\,⟺\\,3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
