    "q-103157": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103157",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Given that $2a≡2b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\nI. $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$\n\nII. $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,10)$\n\nIII. $3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)$",
      "worked_solution": "The division properties of modular arithmetic state the following:\n\n- For $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\n- For $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1,$ we have \n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Applying the first property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a & ≡2b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,10) \\\\ 2\\cdot a & ≡2\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2\\cdot 5) \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{2}\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{2}\\cdot 5) \\\\ a & ≡b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. By statement I and the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)\\,⟺\\,3a≡3b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
