    "q-77147": {
      "dom_id": "step-q77147",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Given that $2a≡2b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,14),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\nI. $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$\n\nII. $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,14)$\n\nIII. $5a≡5b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)$",
      "worked_solution": "The division properties of modular arithmetic state the following:\n\n- For $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\n- For $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1,$ we have \n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. Applying the first property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a & ≡2b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,14) \\\\ 2\\cdot a & ≡2\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,2\\cdot 7) \\\\ \\cancel{2}\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{2}\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{2}\\cdot 7) \\\\ a & ≡b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. By statement I and the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)\\,⟺\\,5a≡5b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-77147-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I and II only",
              "html": "I and II only"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-77147-b",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "II and III only",
              "html": "II and III only"
            },
            {
