    "q-77150": {
      "dom_id": "step-q77150",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Given that $6a≡6b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,9),$ which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\nI. $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6)$\n\nII. $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$\n\nIII. $7a≡7b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)$",
      "worked_solution": "The division properties of modular arithmetic state the following:\n\n- For $k\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\n- For $\\text{gcd}(k,n)=1,$ we have \n\n$$\nka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Applying the first property, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6a & ≡6b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,9) \\\\ 3\\cdot 2\\cdot a & ≡3\\cdot 2\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,3\\cdot 3) \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot 2\\cdot a & ≡\\cancel{3}\\cdot 2\\cdot b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,\\cancel{3}\\cdot 3) \\\\ 2a & ≡2b &  & (\\text{mod}\\,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $gcd(2,3)=1,$  by the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n2a≡2b\\text{ mod }3\\,⟺\\,a≡b\\text{ mod }3\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. By statement II and the second property, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\\,⟺\\,7a≡7b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-77150-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I only",
              "html": "I only"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
